<title>USA: TWA, Boeing sued over July 17 crash.</title>
<headline>TWA, Boeing sued over July 17 crash.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said on Monday that it and Boeing Co were named in a suit filed in New York alleging mechanical malfunction and negligence in connection with the July 17 crash of a TWA Boeing 747 aircraft off Long Island.</p>
<p>A TWA spokesman said &quot;Our position on it is that the National Transportation Safety Board and the Federal Bureau of Intesitation have spent tens of thousands of hours and are unable to support that theory -- or any other theory.&quot;</p>
<p>All the facts have not yet been determined, he added.</p>
<p>The crash killed 230 passengers and crew members.</p>
</text>
